          prompt: 'Describe the function of the following structures of the ear: (a) tympanic membrane (eardrum) (b) ossicles (c) oval window.',
          answer:
            '(a) The tympanic membrane vibrates in response to incoming sound waves, converting airborne pressure waves into mechanical vibration. (b) The ossicles (three small bones — malleus, incus and stapes) transmit and mechanically amplify these vibrations across the middle ear. (c) The oval window is a membrane-covered opening that receives the amplified vibrations from the ossicles and transmits them into the fluid of the cochlea.',
