          answer: 'A test cross is a cross between an individual showing the dominant phenotype (whose genotype is unknown, i.e. it could be homozygous dominant or heterozygous) and an individual known to be homozygous recessive, used to determine the unknown individual’s genotype based on the phenotypes of the offspring produced.',
