          explanation: 'This shows that meiosis and fertilisation are complementary processes that must work together: meiosis halves the chromosome number, and fertilisation restores it, and without meiosis specifically performing this halving step beforehand, sexual reproduction would cause the chromosome number to double indefinitely with each generation.',
