          explanation: 'This is why chromosomal conditions caused by non-disjunction (such as Down syndrome) are statistically more common in pregnancies of women of advanced maternal age, since the underlying cause (an error during meiosis in the egg) becomes progressively more likely the longer that particular egg cell has been held in its long-suspended meiotic state.',
