          explanation: 'These three neuron types together make up a complete, simple reflex pathway: sensory neuron (receptor to CNS) → relay neuron (within the CNS) → motor neuron (CNS to effector), though some very simple reflexes (such as the knee-jerk reflex) bypass the relay neuron entirely.',
