          explanation: 'This adjustable component of total refractive power (provided specifically by the changeable lens, working together with the ciliary muscles and suspensory ligaments) is what gives the normal human eye the ability to focus clearly across a wide range of object distances, rather than being fixed at only one particular distance.',
