          prompt: 'Explain the main similarity between meiosis II and mitosis.',
          answer: 'In both meiosis II and mitosis, sister chromatids of each chromosome are separated from each other and move to opposite poles of the cell, without any further halving of the chromosome number (the cell entering each division already has the chromosome number it will have after that division completes).',
