          answer: 'A vestigial structure is a reduced, often non-functional (or much less functional) anatomical structure that was fully functional in an organism’s ancestors, but has lost most or all of its original function over evolutionary time.',
          explanation: 'The human appendix and coccyx (tailbone) are commonly cited examples of vestigial structures in humans, both inherited from ancestors in which the equivalent structure was fully functional.',
