          prompt: 'Define convergent evolution.',
          answer: 'Convergent evolution is the independent evolution of similar characteristics (such as a similar structure or body shape) in unrelated (or only very distantly related) species, typically as a result of facing similar environmental pressures.',
          explanation: 'Convergent evolution produces analogous structures (such as the wings of a bird and the wings of an insect), which resemble each other in function or superficial form without sharing a recent common origin.',
