          answer: 'The gene pool of a population is the complete collection of all the alleles for all the genes present among all the individuals of that population, at a given point in time.',
          explanation: 'Evolution, at the population level, can be described as a change in the composition (allele frequencies) of a population’s gene pool from one generation to the next.',
