          answer: 'Exponential (J-shaped) growth describes a population that keeps growing at a constantly accelerating rate, with no levelling off, typically occurring when resources are effectively unlimited relative to the population’s size. Sigmoid (S-shaped) growth describes a population whose growth rate slows as it approaches the environment’s carrying capacity, eventually levelling off at a relatively stable population size, reflecting the realistic effect of limited resources.',
