          explanation: 'Acid rain can damage plant life directly, leach essential nutrients out of the soil while releasing toxic metal ions (such as aluminium) previously bound in the soil, and lower the pH of the lakes and rivers it drains into, harming aquatic organisms sensitive to changes in pH.',
