          answer: 'The trachea divides into two bronchi, one entering each lung, which then branch repeatedly into progressively narrower tubes called bronchioles; the smallest bronchioles eventually lead to clusters of alveoli. The bronchi and larger bronchioles carry air deeper into the lungs, with their walls containing rings or plates of cartilage (which decrease further into the smaller bronchioles) that help keep the airways open.',
