          answer: 'A body divided into a series of similar, repeating segments (metameric segmentation), visible as ring-like divisions along the length of the body.',
          explanation: 'Annelida includes earthworms, leeches and various marine bristle worms, all sharing this basic segmented body plan, even though the segments may become more or less specialised between different species within the phylum.',
