          answer: '(1) A prokaryotic cell lacks a true, membrane-bound nucleus, with its genetic material lying free within the cytoplasm instead. (2) A prokaryotic cell lacks membrane-bound organelles, such as mitochondria or chloroplasts. Prokaryotic organisms are classified within the kingdom Monera.',
          explanation: 'These two features (no true nucleus, no membrane-bound organelles) represent a fundamentally simpler level of cellular organisation than that found in the eukaryotic cells of organisms in the other four kingdoms, and are used as the primary basis for separating Monera from the rest of the classification system.',
