          explanation: 'This is why incomplete or inconsistent antibiotic use by individual patients, not only overuse of antibiotics in general, is considered an important contributing factor to the wider development of antibiotic-resistant bacteria, since each incomplete course provides another opportunity for partially resistant survivors to multiply.',
