          marks: 4,
          prompt: 'Describe the functions of the filament and the style in a flower.',
          answer: 'The filament is the thin stalk of the stamen (male reproductive structure) that supports and raises the anther, positioning it where its pollen can most effectively be picked up by a pollinator or carried by wind. The style is the narrow, stalk-like part of the carpel (female reproductive structure) connecting the stigma to the ovary, through which the pollen tube grows down toward the ovule after pollination.',
