          answer: 'Photosynthesis is the process by which chlorophyll-containing organisms trap light energy and use it to convert carbon dioxide and water into glucose, releasing oxygen as a by-product.',
          explanation: 'Virtually all of the chemical energy used by living organisms, including those that cannot photosynthesise themselves, can ultimately be traced back to this single reaction capturing solar energy.',
