          prompt: 'Name the product formed when a human muscle cell respires anaerobically.',
          answer: 'Lactic acid.',
          explanation: 'This differs from the products formed by anaerobically respiring yeast (ethanol and carbon dioxide), showing that different organisms can carry out anaerobic respiration in different ways, despite starting from the same glucose molecule.',
