          explanation: 'This graph illustrates the same limiting-factor principle from the opposite perspective to a light-intensity graph: here carbon dioxide is varied while light intensity is held constant at two different levels, showing that whichever factor supplies the smaller amount at a given moment sets the ceiling on the rate actually achieved.',
