          answer: '(1) The body is divided into a series of similar, repeating ring-like segments (metameric segmentation) along its length. (2) Each segment typically contains its own repeated set of internal structures (such as excretory organs), and the body is often covered by a thin, moist cuticle that assists with gas exchange.',
