          marks: 2,
          prompt: 'Distinguish between a population and a community, in ecological terms.',
          answer: 'A population is a group of individuals of the same species living in the same area at the same time. A community is all of the different populations of different species living and interacting together within that same area at that time.',
          explanation: 'A community exists at a broader level than a single population, since it encompasses every interacting species-population present in a given area, not just one species considered on its own.',
