          difficulty: 'Easy',
          marks: 2,
          prompt: 'Name the blood vessel that carries filtered (relatively clean) blood away from each kidney.',
          answer: 'The renal vein.',
          explanation: 'Blood enters each kidney via the renal artery (carrying blood still containing urea and other wastes) and leaves via the renal vein, once these substances have been removed by the nephrons.',
