          prompt: 'A population of 350 warthogs experiences 56 births, 21 deaths, 14 individuals immigrating into the population, and 7 individuals emigrating out of the population over one year. Calculate (a) the net change in population size, and (b) the population growth rate as a percentage, over that year.',
          answer: '(a) Net change = +42 individuals (final population = 392)  (b) Growth rate = 12.0%',
          explanation: '(a) Net change = (births − deaths) + (immigration − emigration) = (56 − 21) + (14 − 7) = 35 + 7 = 42. (b) Growth rate = (net change ÷ initial population) × 100 = (42 ÷ 350) × 100 = 12.0%.',
